From: bigjakk <6015188+bigjakk@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 12:00:00 -0500
Subject: kcc: label each passthrough texture once instead of on every bind

Stock behaviour
---------------
gpu/command_buffer/service/gles2_cmd_decoder_passthrough_doers.cc,
GLES2DecoderPassthroughImpl::DoBindTexture(): after a successful
glBindTexture of a non-zero texture the decoder unconditionally does

  const char* label = ContextTypeToLabel(feature_info_->context_type());
  api()->glObjectLabelKHRFn(GL_TEXTURE, service_id, strlen(label), label);

There is no feature, workaround or extension gate (GL_KHR_debug is a hard
requirement of the passthrough decoder, see FAIL_INIT_IF_NOT(...khr_debug)
in gles2_cmd_decoder_passthrough.cc). The label is one of "WEBGL1",
"WEBGL2", "OPENGLES2", "OPENGLES3" (context_creation_attribs.cc). It was
added upstream in 90a7dc41c3b0 "Add labeling for passthrough command
decoder GL textures" (M95, crbug 1164111); it is purely diagnostic: ANGLE
keeps the string in gl::TextureState::mLabel and the D3D11 back end turns
it into the D3D debug object name. Nothing in Chromium or ANGLE reads it
back for behaviour.

Cost of one call in ANGLE (src/libANGLE at the pinned revision): GL entry
point + validation (texture lookup, label length), Context::objectLabel()
builds a std::string, Texture::setLabel() copies it, and on D3D11
TextureD3D::onLabelUpdate() -> TextureStorage::setLabel() (another copy) ->
TextureStorage11_*::onLabelUpdate() -> Resource11Base::setKHRDebugLabel()
-> d3d11::SetDebugName(), which concatenates "ANGLE_<internal>_<label>"
(over the small-string limit, so heap allocations) and calls
ID3D11DeviceChild::SetPrivateData(WKPDID_D3DDebugObjectName, ...) on the
texture (and on the swizzle texture if there is one). The Metal and GL
back ends do not override onLabelUpdate(), so there it is only the front
end work.

ANGLE stores the label on the gl::Texture and passes it to every texture
storage it creates later (TextureD3D::*createTextureStorage*(...,
mState.getLabel())), so repeating the call after the first one changes
nothing.

Change
------
With KccLabelTexturesOnce enabled, DoBindTexture() records on the
TexturePassthrough object which label it last applied (an int tag: the
ContextType value, -1 = none) and only calls glObjectLabel when the tag
differs. In practice that is once per texture; if the same TexturePassthrough
is bound by decoders of different context types (shared images, share
groups) it is relabelled whenever the type changes, so the label ANGLE ends
up holding is always the one stock would have left there.

The bookkeeping lives on TexturePassthrough (texture_manager.h) rather than
in a per-decoder set of service ids because that object has the lifetime of
the GL texture: it is created on first bind (or by the shared image
backing), dropped from texture_object_map in DoDeleteTextures, and replaced
wholesale on context loss. A service id reused after deletion gets a new
TexturePassthrough and is therefore labelled again; nothing has to be
cleaned up.

Why it matters here
-------------------
A Windows trace of the game shows the GPU main thread 67-74% busy with
about 282 us per frame in WebGL command decoding. three.js rebinds textures
for every material change, and each bind currently pays for a D3D
SetPrivateData plus several allocations that have no effect.

Gating / A-B
------------
base::Feature KccLabelTexturesOnce, disabled by default, file-local, read
once (function-local static) in DoBindTexture. With it off the call sequence
is the stock one.
  --enable-features=KccLabelTexturesOnce
Measure GPU-process main-thread time per frame (trace category gpu, or the
GLES2DecoderPassthroughImpl::DoCommands slices) and FPS uncapped, on
Windows/D3D11. Expect little or nothing on macOS (Metal) and Linux (GL),
where only the ANGLE front-end call is saved.

Platforms: all (the decoder is shared). Benefit is mainly Windows.

Not verified
------------
- Nothing was compiled.
- Android only: TexturePassthrough::BindToServiceId() can repoint an object
  at another service id; the tag is not reset there, so with the feature on
  such a texture would keep its old tag. Not a KCC platform.
- crbug 1164111 could not be read; the purpose above is from the commit
  subject and from what ANGLE does with the label.

diff --git a/gpu/command_buffer/service/gles2_cmd_decoder_passthrough_doers.cc b/gpu/command_buffer/service/gles2_cmd_decoder_passthrough_doers.cc
index 982aa58bd32611f12f50e3c476c25fa02eb5ea25..546ca66ef6f0453c88809b17d889eb78bc7b051f 100644
--- a/gpu/command_buffer/service/gles2_cmd_decoder_passthrough_doers.cc
+++ b/gpu/command_buffer/service/gles2_cmd_decoder_passthrough_doers.cc
@@ -9,6 +9,7 @@
 #include "base/check.h"
 #include "base/bits.h"
 #include "base/compiler_specific.h"
+#include "base/feature_list.h"
 #include "base/functional/callback_helpers.h"
 #include "base/memory/raw_ptr.h"
 #include "base/notimplemented.h"
@@ -46,6 +47,12 @@ namespace gles2 {
 
 namespace {
 
+// KCC: DoBindTexture() re-applies the context-type debug label
+// (glObjectLabel) on every bind of a non-zero texture. With this feature the
+// label is applied only when it differs from the one last applied to that
+// texture object, i.e. normally once per texture.
+BASE_FEATURE(kKccLabelTexturesOnce, base::FEATURE_DISABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
+
 template <typename ClientType, typename ServiceType, typename GenFunction>
 error::Error GenHelper(GLsizei n,
                        const volatile ClientType* client_ids,
@@ -509,9 +516,14 @@ error::Error GLES2DecoderPassthroughImpl::DoBindTexture(GLenum target,
   scoped_refptr<TexturePassthrough> texture_passthrough;
 
   if (service_id != 0) {
+    static const bool label_once =
+        base::FeatureList::IsEnabled(kKccLabelTexturesOnce);
+
     // Label the texture with additional context info
     const char* label = ContextTypeToLabel(feature_info_->context_type());
-    api()->glObjectLabelKHRFn(GL_TEXTURE, service_id, strlen(label), label);
+    if (!label_once) {
+      api()->glObjectLabelKHRFn(GL_TEXTURE, service_id, strlen(label), label);
+    }
 
     // Create a new texture object to track this texture
     if (!resources_->texture_object_map.GetServiceID(texture,
@@ -524,6 +536,18 @@ error::Error GLES2DecoderPassthroughImpl::DoBindTexture(GLenum target,
       // target than the one it was just bound to
       DCHECK(texture_passthrough->target() == target);
     }
+
+    if (label_once) {
+      // The label is a function of the context type alone, so remember on the
+      // texture object which one it carries and skip the GL call when it would
+      // not change anything. A TexturePassthrough lives exactly as long as its
+      // GL texture, so a reused service id starts out unlabelled again.
+      const int label_tag = static_cast<int>(feature_info_->context_type());
+      if (texture_passthrough->kcc_label_tag() != label_tag) {
+        api()->glObjectLabelKHRFn(GL_TEXTURE, service_id, strlen(label), label);
+        texture_passthrough->set_kcc_label_tag(label_tag);
+      }
+    }
   }
 
   BoundTexture* bound_texture =
diff --git a/gpu/command_buffer/service/texture_manager.h b/gpu/command_buffer/service/texture_manager.h
index c4be683cfbffda1865ec6395bfe1ed8e1c8494ec..23e1dd6c866383ee83cc24a01176b223d8bd2c10 100644
--- a/gpu/command_buffer/service/texture_manager.h
+++ b/gpu/command_buffer/service/texture_manager.h
@@ -76,6 +76,13 @@ class GPU_GLES2_EXPORT TexturePassthrough final
   void SetEstimatedSize(size_t size);
   size_t estimated_size() const { return estimated_size_; }
 
+  // KCC (KccLabelTexturesOnce): identifies the debug label that
+  // GLES2DecoderPassthroughImpl::DoBindTexture last applied to this texture,
+  // so that an identical label is not applied again on every bind. -1 means
+  // no label has been applied through that path yet.
+  int kcc_label_tag() const { return kcc_label_tag_; }
+  void set_kcc_label_tag(int tag) { kcc_label_tag_ = tag; }
+
  protected:
   ~TexturePassthrough() override;
 
@@ -87,6 +94,8 @@ class GPU_GLES2_EXPORT TexturePassthrough final
   bool have_context_;
 
   size_t estimated_size_ = 0;
+
+  int kcc_label_tag_ = -1;
 };
 
